<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέθηπα</span></b> , pf. with pres.
		sense, 
			Ep.
		
		plpf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτεθήπεα</span> as impf., from
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταφ-</span> (v. fin.), of which no
			pres. is found:—poet. Verb, also used in 
			Ion.
		 and late Prose: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> intr.,
				<i>to be astonished, astounded, amazed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός μοι ἐνὶ στήθεσσι τέθηπεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.105
				</span></i>
			; mostly in part.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθηπώς</span>, <i>amazed,
			astonished</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.243
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.64
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				6.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				17.21
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτεθήπεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.166
				</span></i>
			: joined with the part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέθηπα ἀκούων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.156
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				42
			</span></i>.--To this belongs also aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτᾰφον</span>, used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰφών</span>, in the phrases 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταφὼν ἀνόρουσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.193
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.12
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆ δὲ ταφών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.545
				</span></i>
			, al.; later in indic., 3sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάφε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.95
				</span></i>
			, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				B.
				16.86
			</span></i>; 3pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάφον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.207
			</span></i>; 1sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔταφον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					999
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.
			acc., <i>wonder</i> or <i>be amazed at</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.24e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				28
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				56
			</span></i>, etc. (in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.168
			</span></i>, the acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σε</span> belongs only to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαμαι</span>). (Prob. cogn. with
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμβος</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
